Regulation B requires a statement of the specific principal reasons for adverse action; the reasons must relate to and accurately describe the factors actually considered or scored. Statements that the decision was based on internal standards or policies, or on failing to achieve a qualifying score, are insufficient (12 CFR 1002.9(b)(2)). The CFPB has stated that model complexity does not change these obligations (Circulars 2022-03 and 2023-03).

